  "generated_text": "<|channel|>analysis<|message|>Need to parse first int n, then n ints. Compute sum of squares. Return str with newline. Simple. Ensure handles extra whitespace. No constraints.<|end|><|start|>assistant<|channel|>final<|message|>```python\ndef solution(input_str):\n    # Split on whitespace, filter empty\n    parts = [p for p in input_str.split() if p]\n    if not parts:\n        return ''\n    # First part is n, but we don't need to enforce it strictly\n    try:\n        n = int(parts[0])\n    except:\n        n = 0\n    # The rest are the numbers\n    nums = []\n    for p in parts[1:]:\n        try:\n            nums.append(int(p))\n        except:\n            pass\n    # If n is larger than actual count, just use all parsed\n    if n < len(nums):\n        nums = nums[:n]\n    # Sum squares\n    total = sum(x*x for x in nums)\n    return str(total) + '\\n'\n```<|return|>",
